Interpretation
--------------
cp2 SFOCAL1     : Six iterations (PGA gain {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32}), each with a
                  pre-cal baseline, INPMUX=0xFF before SFOCAL1, defensive
                  register re-write after. All six PASS.

                  Gain=1 is the cleanest case: pre_mean 739 µV, predicted
                  OFCAL 0x0004D8 = +1240, actual OFCAL 0x0004D8 = +1240
                  (identical), post_mean -0.040 µV (essentially zero), 100%
                  reduction. The chip's SFOCAL1 cancels the pre-PGA offset
                  exactly when AINCOM-shorted and SFOCAL1's internal short
                  see the same common-mode level.

                  Gain=2 through 32 show slightly higher actual-vs-predicted
                  divergence (40–70 LSB) and post-cal residual offsets of
                  1–15 µV input-referred. This is the chip's noise floor
                  plus a small systematic — when SFOCAL1 shorts the PGA
                  inputs internally, the common-mode level may differ
                  slightly from AINCOM-shorted measurement, producing a
                  small offset that the cal sees but the measurement
                  doesn't (or vice versa).  Acceptable; all >94% reduction.

cp3 SYGCAL1     : With 0.8·AVDD applied via TDAC differential:
                  - Pre-cal V = 4.167 V (chip's default unity-gain reading,
                    +604 ppm above predicted 4.1645 V — that's the chip's
                    intrinsic gain error)
                  - SYGCAL1 writes FSCAL = 0x400000 × VREF / V_input ≈
                    0x4CCB3E (predicted from measured V).
                  - Actual FSCAL = 0x4CCB44, +6 LSB = 1.4 ppm of FS off
                    from prediction. Essentially exact agreement with the
                    datasheet equation.
                  - Post-cal reading = 5.0000 V (+VREF), 0 ppm error.
                  - Behavior matches datasheet §9.4.9.6: SYGCAL1 normalizes
                    the applied input to read as +VREF after cal. This is
                    NOT what a casual reading of "system gain cal" implies;
                    the test's first version misinterpreted this and
                    failed spuriously — fix landed before this bench run.

INTERFACE       : 0x05 after every one of the 7 calibration commands.
                  No snap-back observed. The legacy-HAT issue documented
                  in ADS1263_H7_Integration_Notes.md §6 does not apply
                  here. Defensive register re-write was performed
                  regardless (POWER, MODE2, INPMUX, REFMUX) and should
                  remain in production firmware as a safety net even
                  though this EVM doesn't need it.


