Bug found and fixed during this session
---------------------------------------
cp3 first version expected SYGCAL1 to write FSCAL such that the post-cal
reading equals the input value. The datasheet (§9.4.9.6) actually says
SYGCAL1 assumes the input IS at positive full-scale and writes FSCAL
to normalize accordingly. So with V_input = 0.8·AVDD ≈ 4.167 V, the
chip wrote FSCAL ≈ 1.2× (= 0x4CCCCC nominal) such that the applied
signal would be interpreted as +VREF = 5.0 V. The first-run cp3 saw
post-cal reading 5.0000 V (not the expected 4.16 V) and FAILed.

Test was rewritten to verify the correct datasheet behavior:
  - FSCAL_post must match 0x400000 × VREF / V_measured (the cal math)
  - Post-cal reading must equal +VREF (cal coefficient applied to ADC)
  - INTERFACE register must survive

Memory note saved to spaces/memory/ads1263_sygcal1_normalizes_to_vref.md
so future agents don't rediscover this trap.
